  <prompt>Close Phase 5: end-to-end attestation seam tests (event-log lifecycle -> replay answer at the seam) and the architecture documentation of the attestation model — event log + replay + versioning + the no-materialization rule + the coverage boundary + known gaps (GDPR, retention inheritance, pre-history incompleteness).</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. ADR-038 seam testing; docs-architecture conventions. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>Seam tests proving the project's success criterion 9 (point-in-time attestation answerable) through the public surfaces (endpoints/entry points, not internals); an attestation section in the canonical access-control architecture doc; both green/merged.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>spec.md FR-32 + success criterion 9; design.md §7. The unit-level replay tests live in 082; this task proves the WHOLE chain at the seam: a real grant via the real endpoint produces an event, and replay over that history answers correctly — plus the documentation that makes the mechanism maintainable (the versioning policy is a behavioural contract future evaluator changes must honor).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">tests/integration/seam/ (extend the existing suite with attestation seam tests per suite convention)</file>
      <file role="modify">docs/architecture/uac-access-control.md (or canonical successor — the doc task 058 updated)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/unified-access-control-r2/notes/phase5-evaluator-versioning.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="081" status="pending">Event hooks.</dependency>
      <dependency task="082" status="pending">Replay + versioning.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">KEEP-path seam tests; MAINTAIN-class (they pin the attestation contract); scope: whole task.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md-§2">Docs cite implementing files; known gaps stated as gaps, not omitted. Scope: doc section.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Tests use only public surfaces (endpoints/entry points) — no reaching into the appender or historical source directly. Scope: test design.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
