  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">End-to-end: grant via endpoint on T1, revoke on T2 (fixture-clocked), replay(T1) shows the principal with the granted level and provenance; replay(T3) shows None — all via public surfaces.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Deny lifecycle: deny-add/remove events replay correctly across their boundaries.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: replay for a date before recorded history returns the explicit-incomplete marker (asserted at the seam).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no test (and no code path it exercises) creates a derived-access row — schema-level assertion that only sprk_accessevent rows were written.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The architecture doc's attestation section exists, cites files, and states the GDPR/retention/pre-history gaps.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Full suite green in CI.</criterion>
